// Sev1: fires on any sessions-hub D1 capacity rejection in the last hour, i.e.
// a D1 database (or the account's D1 storage) is full and the hub can no
// longer persist uploads/heartbeats.
//
// Capacity set: the `capacity` class of infra/cf/d1-batch-atomicity.mjs —
// SQLITE_FULL, `database or disk is full`, `Exceeded maximum DB size`, and
// `Your account has exceeded D1's maximum account storage limit`.
//
// Only D1-originated text is matched, never a whole raw Body: hub lines such
// as access.upload / access.multipart_* embed collector-controlled relpaths in
// their R2 keys, and collector.event carries a collector-controlled payload, so
// a Body-wide match would let any enrolled machine forge this Sev1. Two shapes
// carry the error, both anchored at the start of the D1 message, as the queue
// consumer's own `message.startsWith('D1_ERROR')` check does:
//   1. Bare Workers runtime exception lines whose whole Body starts with
//      `D1_ERROR` (no JSON, no event). 21,091 of the 21,697 capacity lines in
//      the 2026-11-12 outage had this shape (`D1_ERROR: Exceeded maximum DB size`).
//   2. The `error` field of ANY structured hub event except collector.event and
//      access.*. Every hub emitter that logs a caught failure does so as
//      `error: String(e)` (hub/src: parse.error, parse.export.transient,
//      hub.index_catalog.sync_failed, hub.certs.*, hub.watchdog.warn, ...), so
//      a D1 failure there reads `Error: D1_ERROR: ...` or `D1_ERROR: ...`. An
//      IDX shard or catalog DB filling while main is healthy surfaces only here
//      (no bare lines). Outage counts: parse.error 603, pricing 3.
// parse-errors.kql excludes the same D1-anchored capacity set, so the outage
// pages here at Sev1 instead.
//
// Window 1h, evaluated every 15m (provision.sh): the overlap tolerates
// OTLP/DCR ingestion delay at evaluation boundaries; the alert is stateful.
// `contains` (substring, case-insensitive), not `has`: `has` is term-based and
// does not reliably match multi-word phrases. A bare summarize always yields
// one row, so `where lines > 0` drops it on a healthy window; otherwise that
// one compact row trips provision.sh's `count > 0`. Missing OTelLogs degrades
// to empty.
let otel = union isfuzzy=true
    (datatable(TimeGenerated:datetime, Body:string, ServiceName:string)[]),
    (OTelLogs | project TimeGenerated, Body, ServiceName);
otel
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
| where ServiceName == 'sessions-hub'
| where Body contains "D1_ERROR"
| extend body = todynamic(Body)
| extend event = tostring(body.event)
| extend d1_error = case(
    Body startswith_cs "D1_ERROR", Body,
    isnotempty(event) and event != "collector.event" and not(event startswith_cs "access."), tostring(body.error),
    "")
| where d1_error startswith_cs "D1_ERROR" or d1_error startswith_cs "Error: D1_ERROR"
| where d1_error contains "SQLITE_FULL"
    or d1_error contains "database or disk is full"
    or d1_error contains "Exceeded maximum DB size"
    or d1_error contains "exceeded D1's maximum account storage limit"
| summarize lines = count(), first_at = min(TimeGenerated), last_at = max(TimeGenerated),
    samples = make_set(substring(Body, 0, 300), 5)
| where lines > 0
